     "Dear all,\r<br>\r<br>I am plotting a geom_line plot. My intention is to plot a line and get the parts of the graph that correspond to significant p-values either ’thicker’ or highlight them somehow (dots or else).\r<br>\r<br>ggplot(my.data, aes(Year,MoranI,colour=factor(Type)))+\r<br>  geom_line(mapping=aes(y=MoranI),size=0.6,linetype=1)+\r<br> \r<br>  labs(title = &quot;&quot;, x = &quot;&quot;, y = &quot;&quot;) +\r<br>  scale_x_continuous(breaks=c(1981,1985,1990,1995,2000),limits=c(1981,2000))+\r<br>\r<br>  scale_colour_manual(name = &#39;Contiguity&#39;, \r<br>                      values = rainbow(2, s = 1, v = 1, start = 0, end = max(1, 2 - 1)/2, alpha = 1),\r<br>                      labels=label_select\r<br>                      )+\r<br>  scale_fill_discrete(name=&quot;legendName&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>where: \r<br>p.value_logical =0 if the p-value is significant and 1 otherwise\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>Any help on the issue will be greatly appreciated!\r<br>\r<br>Best regards,\r<br>\r<br>Ale\r<br>\r<br>reproducible sample:\r<br>\r<br>my.data&lt;–structure(list(Age = c(25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, \r<br>25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, \r<br>25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, \r<br>25L, 25L), Type = c(23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, \r<br>23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 23L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, \r<br>25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, 25L, \r<br>25L), Year = c(1981L, 1982L, 1983L, 1984L, 1985L, 1986L, 1987L, \r<br>1988L, 1989L, 1990L, 1991L, 1992L, 1993L, 1994L, 1995L, 1996L, \r<br>1997L, 1998L, 1981L, 1982L, 1983L, 1984L, 1985L, 1986L, 1987L, \r<br>1988L, 1989L, 1990L, 1991L, 1992L, 1993L, 1994L, 1995L, 1996L, \r<br>1997L, 1998L), MoranI = c(0.212263626, 0.202790521, 0.169931088, \r<br>0.237828001, 0.27097048, 0.525170195, 0.355569798, 0.372083659, \r<br>0.390228718, 0.393121392, 0.358869702, 0.349731047, 0.394278365, \r<br>0.377251669, 0.31716243